# Rule: Landing v7

When editing these paths, you are in a **layered composite** (fixed `.gateway`, sticky hero, opaque stations) — not a flat page.

**Read first:** `sentinel/decisions/008-landing-v7-background-layers.md`, `sentinel/decisions/010-brandmark-choreography.md`, `sentinel/decisions/031-rail-manifest.md`, `sentinel/decisions/033-arc-cases-orbit.md` (orbit superseded; funnel live), `sentinel/decisions/034-arc-cases-terrace.md` (superseded by ADR-035), `sentinel/decisions/035-arc-cases-terminal.md` (reveal surface superseded by ADR-036), `sentinel/decisions/036-arc-cases-card.md` (the live cases reveal; §3/§5 superseded by ADR-041), `sentinel/decisions/041-arc-cases-sigil.md` (the live trigger + ordering), `.claude/skills/landing-v7-compositing/SKILL.md`, `.claude/skills/brandmark-choreography/SKILL.md`.

**Funnel (ADR-033):** hero → corridor (thesis + Arc) → services → about →
continuum → practice → contact. `#tools`/`#build` retired — the four
production cases live ONLY on the Arc's Build-park cases reveal
(click-armed via the CUE — a dotted-leader + label docked under the Build title,
ADR-042; the node streams fold onto an in-canvas 3D tools card's slab edges and
the card then materializes into the frame they made, no camera move — ADR-036 +
ADR-041 + ADR-042). Order is owned by the parse arrays in `app/(marketing)/page.tsx`,
in lockstep with `lib/rail-manifest/entries.ts` + the drift-guard tests;
never reorder via prototype-HTML edits. `PROJECT_CASES` is the single
canonical case module; the rest of `tools-cards/` is the
`/test/project-cards` lab's shared core — do not remount it on the
landing.

**Arc Cases is an in-canvas 3D card — no camera channel (ADR-036, supersedes ADR-035).** The cases reveal is `ArcCasesCard`, ONE in-canvas portrait tools card mounted in the gyro assembly (a sibling of `ShellStack`) between the two Build-park stack columns, in front of the sphere; the accessible stepper row `ArcCasesStepper` (◂ 01 02 03 04 ▸ + CLOSE, region id `arc-cases-terminal`) is mounted in `HomeCorridor`. On arm the sources/surfaces DOM labels fade out on `arcCasesLevelRef` (single writer = the card's R3F `useFrame` at priority −5; readers = `gateStackLabel` label fade + the caption-card fade + the stepper's own rAF + `ShellStack`, which folds the source/surface node streams onto the card's actual left/right slab side walls so the screen reads as mounted on the nodes). The ref carries the card's slab edges (`cardEdges`, shell-local — the single source of truth for that mount geometry, direct math, NO viewport unprojection / `panelRect`). The corridor camera is a pure Z dolly through arm/disarm. Gate parity: the JS `ARC_CASES_MEDIA` gate == the CSS hide of BOTH the cue and the stepper. No scroll writer, no scroll lock, no backdrop; inert is reconciled every frame; DOM order = focus order. Do NOT re-introduce a camera channel, the DOM overlay panel, or the `panelRect` unprojection latch.

**The reveal is PHASED (ADR-041, supersedes ADR-036 §3/§5); the trigger is a CUE under the Build title (ADR-042, supersedes ADR-041 §2).** ONE damped arm level, TWO ordered phases: the node fold runs on `arcFoldInput(level)` (complete at `ARC_FOLD_DONE` 0.62 — feed `arcLatchEnvelope` the BARE clamped ratio; it supplies the easing, pre-easing double-eases) and the CARD reads `arcCardPresence(level)` (`smootherstep(0.62, 1)`), published as `cardPresence` on `arcCasesLevelRef` by the same single writer. Beat: **labels fade → nodes fold and latch → card materializes into the frame they made**; close plays it backwards. The card's material opacities / visibility / scale-in / depth-write AND the stepper's opacity+inert all read `cardPresence`, never the raw `level` — the strict invariant (`arcCardPresence === 0` while `arcFoldInput < 1`) is unit-pinned. The sphere sigil is DELETED (ADR-042): the trigger is `ArcCasesCue`, a DOM dotted-leader + label docked UNDER the Build station title (mounted as the Build `StationBlock`'s `afterContent`; it inherits the Build header's per-frame opacity). Its `intelligence.sigil` anchor, `gateSigil`, and `SIGIL_Z` are gone. It keeps the ADR-041 contracts verbatim (aria-controls/expanded, every-frame inert reconciliation, stable callback ref, auto-disarm watcher) and arms only once the notes have SETTLED (`sigilSettle`, `ARC_SIGIL_SETTLE` [0.70, 0.84] on the smoothed stack — **measured against the live corridor; re-measure before retuning**); below the gate it is `inert` + CSS-faded (`.is-armable`). Because it sits at the TOP of the viewport, clear of the centred card, it **stays visible AND interactive while armed** (a 2nd click / Escape closes; Escape refocus falls out for free — it was never inert) — no phantom-click guard, no fade-to-0. The stepper ✕ CLOSE stays. Do NOT retune `ARC_BAND_IN` to "fix" its stale stack comment — the park (0.9225) sits below the accretion peak (0.95), so raising it would gate the card off entirely; sequencing is enforced on the trigger instead. In Playwright the cue rides the Build header's gyro parallax, so `locator.click()` can still flake ("element is not stable") — click at its box centre via `page.mouse.click`.

**Rail manifest (ADR-031; roster ADR-033; left rail Update 9):** the
left-rail manifest skeleton is parse-injected
(`lib/v7-parse/railManifest.ts`) and mutated in place by
`RailManifestController` — never `createRoot` into
`[data-rail-manifest-root]`, keep the prototype shell byte-exact, and
change journey order only in `lib/rail-manifest/entries.ts` (drift-guard
tested). **Update 9 (2026-07-16): the left rail is ONE travelling gold
detent diamond (12px, `.rail-manifest__diamond`, centred on the 2px
track), not the 3-pillar rolodex.** It snaps to a detent per EVERY
`MANIFEST_ENTRIES` entry (+ future interstitials), at BEAT granularity in
the corridor — hero → thesis → Navigate → Encode → Build → sections (the
"arc" entry is retired). Detents are scroll-PROPORTIONAL
(`detentTable.ts` + `scrollTargetForEntry`; corridor beats at their parks,
fractions 0.30/0.48/0.70), recomputed on resize/layout only. Position
(`--rail-diamond-top`) is a pure function of `activeIdx` — never
scroll-scrubbed, no per-frame scroll writer; the 350ms `top` glide is
gated behind `data-ready`; the 13-tick ladder always stays. The active
corridor beat comes from `data-corridor-phase`, now published as
`thesis|navigate|encode|build` (CorridorStationHeaders RAF, hand-offs
`CORRIDOR_BEAT_ENTER` 0.2/0.48/0.78 — mirrors CorridorProgressRail's
STAGES band starts, keep in lockstep). Hover/focus reveals the active
entry's title (hidden `.rail-manifest__title`, gated on `data-has-title`;
`manifestTitle` is `null` for hero + blank-name interstitials). Do NOT
re-add the rolodex reel / 3-pillar roster / terminal bar; `RAIL_ROWS` /
`glyph` are removed. The right rail: `THE ARC · 03`
register during the corridor, `SOURCE BUS · 04` (`ServicesRailRegister`,
services.css) during services — both on the shared `--rail-register-pitch`
grid, active row = gold underline.

**Process:** `sentinel/MAINTENANCE.md` — Cycle B before large section work; Cycle A after non-trivial fixes.
